<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <h1>Órrery configuration</h1>
  <p class="sub">The pipeline as it actually runs, generated from this checkout's canonical files.
     Steps sharing a role share one model, and bounded workflow controls sit at
     the stage they govern.</p>
  <div class="chartwrap" id="chart"></div>
  <div class="scopenote">
    Saving changes the defaults for <strong>new Orrery processes</strong>;
    running sessions are unaffected. A repository's private
    <code>.orrery.json</code> principal override still wins. Every role may use either provider.
    Runtime failure automatically ranks the nearest potential model, but never
    starts it without the user's explicit, candidate-bound approval.
    __CATALOGUE_NOTE__
    Known models expose only the thinking levels reported for that model;
    a custom identifier also requires an explicit provider.
  </div>
  <div class="actions">
    <button id="preview" class="btn btn-primary" type="button">Preview changes</button>
    <button id="apply" class="btn btn-primary" type="button" disabled>Apply</button>
    <button id="revert" class="btn btn-ghost" type="button">Revert edits</button>
    <span class="hint">Nothing is written until you apply.</span>
  </div>
  <div id="result"></div>
